    "DIAGNOSIS": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [],
      "subsections": {
        "DIFFERENTIAL DIAGNOSIS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "DIFFERENTIAL DIAGNOSIS",
          "canonical_heading": "DIFFERENTIAL DIAGNOSIS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Reactive eosinophilia—parasitism, allergic/hypersensitivity reactions, infectious disease, immune-mediated disease, fungal infections, neoplasia; with these conditions, eosinophilia usually limited in magnitude and remains confined to specific organ.",
              "pdf_page": 760,
              "printed_page": 678,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Eosinophilic leukemia—differentiating criteria: eosinophilic leukemia tends to have immature eosinophils seen in higher numbers in circulation, constituting higher percentage of leukocyte differential; anemia more common and often more severe; myeloid : erythroid (M : E) ratio in bone",
              "pdf_page": 760,
              "printed_page": 678,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "marrow higher (>10 : 1) with more immature/",
              "pdf_page": 760,
              "printed_page": 678,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Hydroxyurea—to reduce eosinophil count blast forms and disorderly maturation; tissue if not normal or near normal after 7–14 days infiltrates consist of immature eosinophils and of steroid treatment; used long term if may show sinusoidal pattern in liver without effective in conjunction with steroids. fibrosis; in cats, chloroma-like masses in",
              "pdf_page": 760,
              "printed_page": 678,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Cyclosporine A—suppresses production of kidneys are reported. eosinophilopoietic factors by T cells.",
              "pdf_page": 760,
              "printed_page": 678,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Vincristine and alkylating agents such as",
              "pdf_page": 760,
              "printed_page": 678,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
